    <!-- Rules Sheet -->
    <string name="rules_title">How to Play Odd-Even Cricket</string>
    <string name="rules_toss_heading">1. The Odd-Even Toss</string>
    <string name="rules_toss_body">Call Odd or Even, then throw a number from 1 to 6. If your number plus the CPU\'s number matches your call, you win the toss and decide to Bat or Bowl first.</string>
    <string name="rules_play_heading">2. Batting &amp; Bowling</string>
    <string name="rules_play_body">Every ball, both players pick a number from 1 to 6 simultaneously. If the numbers differ, the batter scores their chosen number in runs. If both numbers match, the batter is OUT!</string>
    <string name="rules_win_heading">3. Winning the Match</string>
    <string name="rules_win_body">Innings end when all wickets fall or overs run out. Chase down the target in the 2nd innings to win — or settle ties with a dramatic Super Over!</string>
    <string name="rules_got_it">Got It</string>
